<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The collar's nullifying, as a gene (2026-09-23). This is what greys out greedy and
		arrogant in a wearer's trait list, and it is the only way to do it: `suppressedTraits`
		exists on GeneDef alone (checked against the generated def schema), so a hediff cannot
		suppress a trait and neither can a code patch - a patch on TraitSet.HasTrait can mute
		the *effects* of a trait, which the first version of this collar did, but the trait
		list on the Social tab still showed them in full colour.

		Granted and removed by Source/Reptiles/WeddingCollar.cs with the hediff, as a
		**xenogene** (the game's own word for an acquired gene, the same kind a gene drug
		gives). Nothing here is cosmetic: the engine reads this list when it decides whether
		the pawn has a trait at all, so vanilla's own trait checks report greedy and arrogant
		absent while she wears the collar, and the trait rows grey out.

		Nothing is forced here: kind and masochistic are really gained, by the hediff's comp,
		because those two have to behave as well as appear. Suppression is one-way - the
		engine can hide a trait, not grant one - which is why the two halves are split.

		The xenotype is untouched: Pawn_GeneTracker keeps the xenotype in a field set at
		generation, so adding or removing an acquired gene leaves the pawn's displayed
		xenotype exactly as it was.

		Icon: Textures/UI/Icons/Genes/PMM_Gene_WeddingCollar.png, the collar itself.
	-->
	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_WeddingCollar</defName>
		<label>wedding collar</label>
		<labelShortAdj>collared</labelShortAdj>
		<description>She wears a wedding collar, and its spell keeps her dragon's pride quiet: while it is on she is neither greedy nor arrogant.</description>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/PMM_Gene_WeddingCollar</iconPath>
		<displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
		<canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
		<biostatCpx>0</biostatCpx>
		<biostatMet>0</biostatMet>
		<suppressedTraits>
			<li><def>Greedy</def></li>
			<li><def>PMM_Arrogant</def></li>
		</suppressedTraits>
	</GeneDef>

</Defs>
